  annotation "note_1771577880686_2", anchor: "some names appear before the deaths they commemorate", text: "The Remembrancers work three levels below the memorial-stones, which places them — if the Nightfall Shelf depth charts I have cross-referenced are accurate — within two strata of late Faction Wars ice-memory. At that depth during any Long Dark thinning, impression bleed from adjacent temporal layers is not speculation; it is well-documented in my catalogue. The names may belong to a stratum the carvers are *reading* rather than *inventing*. Faction Wars dead, surfacing through the tools. That said: the Remembrancers themselves believe the names are *new*. I note this and do not resolve it. Some questions are better left as questions, particularly when the alternative is confirming that the ice knows who dies next.", type: :temporal, display: :full
